---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { site, url } from '../data/site';
const updated = '25 July 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="FinvestLens privacy policy. There is no account, no analytics and no server — your book stays on your device."
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy policy" lead={`Last updated ${updated}`} />

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <div
      class="mb-12 rounded-2xl border border-brand-200 bg-brand-50/60 p-6 dark:border-brand-800/60 dark:bg-brand-900/20"
    >
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-800 dark:text-ink-100">
        <strong>The short version.</strong> FinvestLens has no account to sign up for,
        no analytics, and no server of ours for your data to reach. Your book is a
        file on your device. We never see it, and neither does anyone else.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-doc">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        FinvestLens is published by <a href={site.publisher.url}>{site.publisher.legalName}</a>
        (“we”, “us”). For anything in this policy, write to
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Nothing.</strong> We operate no servers for FinvestLens, run no
        analytics or crash reporting, use no advertising or tracking SDKs, and have
        no way to identify you. The app’s privacy manifest declares no collected data
        types and no tracking domains.
      </p>

      <h2>Where your financial data lives</h2>
      <p>
        Your book is a single file you choose the location of — local disk, iCloud
        Drive, or a network share. It is read and written by the app on your device
        and nowhere else. Attachments you link are likewise files on your storage.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you keep your book in iCloud Drive, it syncs between <em>your own</em>
        devices through your Apple Account, under Apple’s terms and encryption. That
        is a transfer between you and Apple; it does not involve us.
      </p>

      <h2>Apple Intelligence and document reading</h2>
      <p>
        Smart Import, categorisation suggestions, budget proposals and report
        commentary are produced by Apple’s on-device foundation models. The
        statements, invoices and dividend notices you point the app at are processed
        <strong>on your device</strong>. Their contents are not sent to us or to any
        third party by FinvestLens.
      </p>

      <h2>Network requests the app can make</h2>
      <p>
        FinvestLens makes network requests in exactly one situation: when you ask it
        to fetch security prices or exchange rates. Those requests go to the quote
        provider you choose:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Yahoo Finance and Stooq — no account or key required</li>
        <li>EODHD (<code>eodhd.com</code>)</li>
        <li>Alpha Vantage (<code>alphavantage.co</code>)</li>
        <li>Finnhub (<code>finnhub.io</code>)</li>
        <li>Twelve Data (<code>twelvedata.com</code>)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Such a request contains the ticker symbols and date ranges being priced. It
        does not contain your balances, transactions, account names or any personal
        detail. Each provider is an independent company with its own privacy policy,
        which governs what it does with the request.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you never fetch prices, the app makes no network requests at all. It works
        entirely offline.
      </p>

      <h2>API keys and credentials</h2>
      <p>
        Keys for the keyed price providers are stored in the macOS Keychain on the
        device you enter them on. They are never written into your book file and are
        never transmitted anywhere except to the provider they belong to.
      </p>

      <h2>Local authentication</h2>
      <p>
        Where the app asks for Touch ID or your password — to open a protected book,
        or to reach Emergency Records — that check is performed by macOS. FinvestLens
        receives only a yes or no. It never sees your password or biometric data.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        FinvestLens is a general-purpose accounting application, not directed at
        children, and collects no data from anyone.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Rights of access, correction, deletion and portability apply to data a
        publisher holds about you. We hold none. Your own data is in your own file:
        you can read it, change it, export it to GnuCash XML or a Ledger journal, or
        delete the file, all without asking us.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the revised version will be published on this page
        with a new date. Material changes will also be noted in the release notes.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a> ·
        <a href={url('/support/')}>Support</a> ·
        <a href={site.publisher.url}>{site.publisher.legalName}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
